Subject: Bump Apache HttpComponents 5.x for CVE remediation (httpcore5 5.4->5.4.3, httpclient5 5.6.1->5.6.3)
Origin: DHI-internal CVE remediation
Reference: https://repo1.maven.org/maven2/org/apache/httpcomponents/core5/httpcore5/5.4.3/
Description: The sql plugin declares its own resolutionStrategy.force for
  httpcore5, httpcore5-h2 and httpclient5, reading versions.httpcore5 and
  versions.httpclient5 from the OpenSearch version catalog. That force is applied
  when the plugin build script is evaluated, which is after the DHI Gradle init
  script, so it wins over the init script's eachDependency substitution and the
  plugin ships the catalog versions regardless. Bump the catalog itself so the
  plugin's own force resolves the remediated versions; this also covers core.

--- a/gradle/libs.versions.toml
+++ b/gradle/libs.versions.toml
@@ -49,8 +49,8 @@
 reactor           = "3.8.6"
 
 # client dependencies
-httpclient5       = "5.6.1"
-httpcore5         = "5.4"
+httpclient5       = "5.6.3"
+httpcore5         = "5.4.3"
 httpclient        = "4.5.14"
 httpcore          = "4.4.16"
 httpasyncclient   = "4.1.5"
